  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="154">
        <pb n="201"/>
        <head>154 — i — VII. — <quote>Let the redeemed of the Lord say</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>. <quote>Because thou art great and [a doer of<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> wonders</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">On the Holy Homerite Martyrs, Who Were Martyred in the City of <placeName>Nigran</placeName> in the Southern Territories of the Saracens, in the Days of <persName>Justin</persName>, King of the Romans, When the Christians There Were Being Persecuted by <persName>Masruk</persName>, King of the Arabs, Who Was a Jew by Religion, and Forced to Deny <persName>Christ</persName>; the Composition of <persName>John Psaltes</persName>, Archimandrite of the House of <persName>Aphthonia</persName>.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">Who<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> shall tell thy mighty deeds<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/>, <persName>Christ</persName>, God? Lo! even the foreign and barbarous country of the Homerites, having been inflamed by the fear of thee, beheld and imitated the faith of the Cappadocians. <placeName>Sebaste</placeName> in one arena (<foreign xml:lang="grc">στάδιον</foreign>) only consisting of a pool of water in the cold season perfected forty persons by [martyrdom : and <placeName>Nigran</placeName><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/> equalled this and surpassed it five times over, and<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> showed us more than two hundred combatants (<foreign xml:lang="grc">ἀθληταί</foreign>) who gained distinction in con-<pb n="202"/>flict, the first of whom was <persName>Harith</persName> the doctor; who also in our recent times contended in the conflict : by whose prayers [do away<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> offences and stumbling-blocks from within the churches, and defeat and overthrow<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> all heresies, and confirm us in thy faith, and number us among<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a10" target="#n10" n="10"/> thy elect; and deliver us, merciful<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a11" target="#n11" n="11"/> Lord.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 1</orig></choice> Ps. cvii, 2.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 2</orig></choice> B <quote>doest</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 3</orig></choice> Id. lxxxvi, 10 LXX.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 4</orig></choice> Id. cvi, 2 (not quoted).</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>and powerful deeds</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>martyrs : and <placeName>Nigran</placeName>, having</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 201, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>also</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 202, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>still</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 202, n. 2</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>dissolve</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n10" target="#a10" n="10"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 202, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>with</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n11" target="#a11" n="11"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 202, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>who only (art) merciful</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
